"c1-15": [
  { t: "tfng", x: "An advertisement claims: “Nine out of ten dentists recommend Brightsmile toothpaste.” At first glance, this sounds convincing. However, the claim does not reveal how many dentists were asked, or whether they could recommend more than one brand. Furthermore, the survey was paid for by the company itself. A critical reader should therefore treat the statement as a marketing message rather than as sound scientific evidence.", st: ["The advertisement says how many dentists took part in the survey.|F|Bài nói quảng cáo không cho biết đã hỏi bao nhiêu nha sĩ.", "The survey was funded by the toothpaste company.|T", "Brightsmile is the cheapest toothpaste on the market.|NG|Bài không nói gì về giá.", "The writer suggests the claim is not strong scientific evidence.|T"] },
  { t: "dlg", sc: "Hai người tranh luận, một người chỉ ra các lỗi lập luận.", l: ["Jake: We shouldn't listen to Dr. Hill's advice on diet. She's overweight herself.", "Mai: That's an ad hominem argument. Her weight doesn't make her research wrong.", "Jake: Fine. But if we let schools sell fast food, soon kids will be eating nothing else.", "Mai: That's a slippery slope. There's no evidence that one leads to the other.", "Jake: So you're saying children should eat junk food all day?", "Mai: No, that's a straw man. I never said that."], q: ["Why does Mai reject Jake's first argument?|It attacks the person, not the research|It uses incorrect statistics|It is about fast food, not diet", "What fallacy does Mai identify in Jake's second argument?|A slippery slope|A straw man|An ad hominem", "What does Mai mean by “a straw man”?|Jake has misrepresented her view|Jake has attacked her personally|Jake's conclusion is valid"] }
],
"c1-16": [
  { t: "journal", q: "Two sources disagree about whether working from home improves productivity. Write three sentences synthesizing both views.", vi: "Hai nguồn tin trái ngược nhau về việc làm việc tại nhà có tăng năng suất hay không. Viết 3 câu tổng hợp cả hai quan điểm.", kw: ["source/sources/study/report", "whereas/while/however/by contrast/diverge", "both/converge/agree/corroborate"], m: "While one study reports that employees working from home complete more tasks, a second source suggests that collaboration suffers. The two sources diverge mainly because they measure productivity in different ways. However, both agree that flexible arrangements work best when teams still meet in person regularly." },
  { t: "pic", chart: { t: "Workers who say they are more productive at home (%)", d: [["Survey A", 68], ["Survey B", 41]] }, q: "Two surveys asked workers whether they are more productive at home. Compare the results and suggest a reason for the difference.", vi: "Hai cuộc khảo sát hỏi người lao động có làm việc hiệu quả hơn ở nhà không. So sánh kết quả và đưa ra một lý do cho sự khác biệt.", kw: ["whereas/while/by contrast", "diverge/differ/difference", "percent", "might/may/could/possibly/because"], m: "According to Survey A, 68 percent of workers feel more productive at home, whereas only 41 percent say so in Survey B. The two sources clearly diverge. This difference might be because the surveys asked very different groups of workers.", min: 35 }
],

